<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="Syntax">
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`watch(effect)
watch(sources, effect)`} />

        <Section title="Parameters" level={3}>
            <ul>
                <li><code>sources</code> (optional) — one <code>Reactive</code> or an array of them.
                Given, the effect runs only when those change. Two overloads rather than a union:
                the first argument discriminates them.</li>
                <li><code>effect</code> — the function to run. Returning a <code>Disposer</code>
                gives it a teardown.</li>
            </ul>
        </Section>

        <Section title="Return value" level={3}>
            <p>A function that stops the watch.</p>
        </Section>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Members">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>watch</code></td><td><code>(effect: Effect) =&gt; () =&gt; void</code></td><td>Watches whatever the effect reads.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>watch</code></td><td><code>(sources: Reactive&lt;unknown, never, unknown, unknown&gt; | Reactive&lt;unknown, never, unknown, unknown&gt;[], effect: Effect) =&gt; () =&gt; void</code></td><td>The narrowed form, over named sources.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Effect</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; void | Disposer</code></td><td>What runs on change.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Disposer</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; void</code></td><td>What tears down the previous run: before each rerun, and once at teardown.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>flushSync</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; void</code></td><td>Ends the turn: every effect a write woke runs now.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Description">
        <p>A watch registered inside a component is owned by it, and its disposer runs at unmount.
        One registered from a plain <code>.ts</code> module has no owner, so you stop it with the
        returned function.</p>

        <p><strong>A watch reruns on a server too.</strong> A write wakes it at the end of the turn,
        as in a browser, and it reruns under the request it was opened in. The disposer runs when
        that request's scope ends. Same callable, same schedule, on both sides.</p>

        <p>An error in an effect is never silent. A throw from the effect, a throw from the
        disposer, and a read of a failed value inside one all reach <code>onError</code> with the
        trace attached and warn on <code>abide:watch</code>. In a browser a throw from the effect is
        additionally re-thrown, and surfaces as an uncaught error an error reporter sees.</p>

        <p><strong>An effect that threw stops its watch.</strong> One that throws once usually
        throws every run, and a watch rerunning into the same throw is a loop with a log line per
        iteration.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Examples">
        <Section title="An effect over what it reads" level={3}>
            <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`const stop = watch(() => {
    document.title = \`\${unread()} unread\`
})`} />
        </Section>

        <Section title="An effect with a teardown" level={3}>
            <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`watch(() => {
    const id = setInterval(poll, 1000)
    return () => clearInterval(id)
})`} />
        </Section>

        <Section title="An effect narrowed to its sources" level={3}>
            <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`watch([topic], () => analytics.compose(topic(), draft().length))`} />
        </Section>
    </Section>

    <Section title="See also">
        <ul>
            <li><a href={url('/values/do-something-when-a-value-changes')}>Watching values</a></li>
            <li><a href={url('/templates/run-code-when-a-component-loads')}>Scripts</a></li>
            <li><a href={url('/reference/reactive')}><code>Reactive</code></a></li>
        </ul>
    </Section>
</Doc>
